## Why This Is Asked

Tests offline-first sync design, conflict resolution, and native bridge considerations. Evaluates real-world trade-offs between consistency models and performance.

## Key Concepts

- **Offline-first sync architecture**: Prioritizes local-first writes with eventual consistency to remote
- **TurboModule/JSI bridges**: Enables synchronous, type-safe native communication without bridge serialization overhead
- **Local SQLite queue**: Tracks pending changes with timestamps and operation types for reliable sync
- **Conflict resolution strategies**: Version vectors for causality tracking; CRDT or last-write-wins for merge semantics
- **Schema migrations**: Additive migrations with backward compatibility; migration scripts stored in versioned history table
- **Background workers**: Dedicated threads prevent UI jank during heavy I/O operations
- **Backpressure handling**: Bounded queue sizes with configurable flush thresholds

## Code Example

```javascript
import { startSync, pauseSync, resumeSync, stopSync, getSyncStatus } from '@app/sync';

await startSync('https://api.example.com/sync', {
  pollMs: 30000,
  backoff: { initial: 1000, max: 60000, jitter: 0.3 },
  onRecordSynced: (record) => console.log('Synced:', record.id),
  onRemoteChange: (changes) => applyRemoteChanges(changes),
});

// UI indicator
const status = getSyncStatus();
console.log(`Pending: ${status.pending}, Last sync: ${status.lastSyncAt}`);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical React Native fundamentals: data fetching, local persistence, list rendering performance, and graceful error handling in a fintech scenario.

## Key Concepts
- FlatList and RefreshControl for smooth UI
- AsyncStorage offline caching strategy
- Error handling and retry patterns
- Minimal, reusable API surface and prop design

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, {useEffect, useState} from 'react';
import {FlatList, View, Text, Button, ActivityIndicator, RefreshControl} from 'react-native';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';

export default function StockList({endpoint = '/api/stocks', storageKey = 'stocks_cache'}) {
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [refreshing, setRefreshing] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => { loadCache(); fetchData(); }, []);

  async function loadCache() {
    try { const cached = await AsyncStorage.getItem(storageKey); if (cached) setData(JSON.parse(cached)); } catch {}
  }

  async function fetchData() {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(endpoint);
      const json = await res.json();
      setData(json);
      await AsyncStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(json));
    } catch {
      // keep existing data
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
      setRefreshing(false);
    }
  }

  function renderItem({item}) { return (
    <View><Text>{item.symbol} — {item.price}</Text></View>
  ); }

  return (
    data.length ? (
      <FlatList data={data} keyExtractor={i => i.symbol} renderItem={renderItem}
        refreshControl={<RefreshControl refreshing={refreshing} onRefresh={() => { setRefreshing(true); fetchData(); }} />} />
    ) : (
      loading ? <ActivityIndicator /> : <Text>No data</Text>
    )
  );
}
```

